at any time when an opportunity in his/her expressed interest or professional area becomes available. Applications submitted through the online form will remain active for the calendar year in which they are submitted. Salary is established on a per-course basis. These positions are not anticipated to be benefits-eligible. Required Application Materials: To be considered for adjunct teaching opportunities, please complete the online application form and attach a single Word or PDF document that contains your 1) cover letter and 2) resume/CV with 3) contact information for two individuals who can provide letters of recommendation. In your cover letter, be sure to connect your professional experience and teaching strengths/experience as it relates to the courses you are applying to teach. The WVU School of Art & Design instructors are engaging, dynamic, and leaders in their respective fields, so please tell us what you will bring into the classroom to ensure a valuable, interactive learning experience for students. West Virginia University is a place of purpose and community. We take pride in our profound impact on the state of West Virginia and are committed to the personal and professional growth of our employees. From the groundbreaking R1 research at our flagship campus in Morgantown to the career-oriented programs at WVU Potomac State in Keyser, and the technology-intensive programs at WVU Tech in Beckley, the contributions of WVU employees resonate across the state, touching lives and shaping futures. At WVU, you will discover a supportive community that champions work-life balance and fosters a collaborative atmosphere. Our core values \u2014 service, curiosity, respect, accountability and appreciation \u2014 unite us as Mountaineers. Join us at West Virginia University, where your work will make a lasting impact. To learn more about WVU, visit wvu.edu. West Virginia University is an Equal Opportunity Employer. We invite all qualified applicants regardless of race, color, religion, sex, national origin, age, disability, genetic information, or Veteran status. Contact us SHARED SERVICES CUSTOMER CARE Location : 3rd Floor, One Waterfront Place, Morgantown, WV 26501 Phone : (304)-293-6006 Email : sharedservices@mail.wvu.edu Get directions to our office Hours Of Operation Monday - Friday 8 a.m. - 5 p.m. Support by Phone Call: 8 a.m. - 5 p.m. Support by Online Chat: Excluding University holidays Accreditations Web Standards Questions or Comments? \u00a9 2025 West Virginia University. West Virginia University is an Equal Opportunity Employer. Last updated on March 6, 2025. A-Z Site Index Campus Map Jobs Directory Give MyAccess MountaineerTRAK WVU Alert WVU Today WVU Portal WVU on Facebook WVU on Twitter WVU on YouTube"}, "https://wvu.taleo.net/careersection/faculty/jobdetail.ftl?job=28957&lang=en": {"title": "Part-time Adjunct Teaching Positions - Department of History", "description": "Job Description - Part-time Adjunct Teaching Positions - Department of History (28957) Go to the main content section. Skip to main content Careers Talent and Culture Required Postings WVU Home Home Career Opportunities Why WVU Community Information WVU Talent Network Welcome. You are not signed in. | My Account Options My Job Cart | Sign In This service is set to disconnect automatically after {0} minutes of inactivity. Your session will end in {1} minutes. Click OK to reset the timer to {0} minutes. You have been signed out. This service is set to sign out after {0} minutes of inactivity. Job Search My Jobpage Basic Search | Advanced Search | Beginning of the main content section. Return to the home page Printable Format Job Description - Part-time Adjunct Teaching Positions - Department of History (28957) Part-time Adjunct Teaching Positions - Department of History - 28957 Description The Department of History ( https://history.wvu.edu ) at West Virginia University invites applications for Part-time Adjunct Teaching Positions. Areas of need will be determined according to the needs of the department. The successful candidate will be responsible for teaching in-person or online courses in the Department of History\u2019s undergraduate and graduate programs. Applications will be accepted throughout the year and will be considered as openings arise. Salary is established on a per-course basis. Qualifications These positions require a master\u2019s or doctoral degree in History or a closely related discipline, along with evidence of effective teaching at the undergraduate or graduate level. Generally, individuals with a doctoral degree are eligible to teach graduate or undergraduate courses; individuals with a master\u2019s degree are eligible to teach undergraduate courses. Please submit via PDF file (a) a letter of application summarizing your teaching qualifications, (b) your curriculum vitae, including professional certifications and professional experience, and (c) contact information for two individuals who can provide letters of recommendation. West Virginia University is a place of purpose and community. We take pride in our profound impact on the state of West Virginia and are committed to the personal and professional growth of our employees. From the groundbreaking R1 research at our flagship campus in Morgantown to the career-oriented programs at WVU Potomac State in Keyser, and the technology-intensive programs at WVU Tech in Beckley, the contributions of WVU employees resonate across the state, touching lives and shaping futures. At WVU, you will discover a supportive community that champions work-life balance and fosters a collaborative atmosphere. Our core values \u2014 service, curiosity, respect, accountability and appreciation \u2014 unite us as Mountaineers. Join us at West Virginia University, where your work will make a lasting impact. To learn more about WVU, visit wvu.edu . West Virginia University is an Equal Opportunity Employer. We invite all qualified applicants regardless of race, color, religion, sex, national origin, age, disability, genetic information, or Veteran status. Contact us SHARED SERVICES CUSTOMER CARE Location : 3rd Floor, One Waterfront Place, Morgantown, WV 26501 Phone : (304)-293-6006 Email : sharedservices@mail.wvu.edu Get directions to our office Hours Of Operation Monday - Friday 8 a.m. - 5 p.m. Support by Phone Call: 8 a.m. - 5 p.m. Support by Online Chat: Excluding University holidays Accreditations Web Standards Questions or Comments? \u00a9 2025 West Virginia University. West Virginia University is an Equal Opportunity Employer. Last updated on March 6, 2025. A-Z Site Index Campus Map Jobs Directory Give MyAccess MountaineerTRAK WVU Alert WVU Today WVU Portal WVU on Facebook WVU on Twitter WVU on YouTube"}, "https://wvu.taleo.net/careersection/faculty/jobdetail.ftl?job=28956&lang=en": {"title": "Part-time Adjunct Teaching Positions - Department of Chemistry", "description": "Job Description - Part-time Adjunct Teaching Positions - Department of Chemistry (28956) Go to the main content section. Skip to main content Careers Talent and Culture Required Postings WVU Home Home Career Opportunities Why WVU Community Information WVU Talent Network Welcome. You are not signed in. | My Account Options My Job Cart | Sign In This service is set to disconnect automatically after {0} minutes of inactivity. Your session will end in {1} minutes. Click OK to reset the timer to {0} minutes. You have been signed out. This service is set to sign out after {0} minutes of inactivity. Job Search My Jobpage Basic Search | Advanced Search | Beginning of the main content section. Return to the home page Printable Format Job Description - Part-time Adjunct Teaching Positions - Department of Chemistry (28956) Part-time Adjunct Teaching Positions - Department of Chemistry - 28956 Description The Department of Chemistry ( https://www.chemistry.wvu.edu/ ) at West Virginia University invites applications for Part-time Adjunct Teaching Positions. Areas of need include, but may not be limited to, classroom and laboratory courses in Preparative Chemistry, General Chemistry, and Organic Chemistry. The successful candidate will be responsible for teaching in-person or online courses in the Department of Chemistry\u2019s undergraduate and graduate programs. Applications will be accepted throughout the year and will be considered as openings arise. Salary is established on a per-course basis. Qualifications These positions require a master\u2019s or doctoral degree in Chemistry or a related discipline (including but not limited to Biochemistry, Chemical Engineering, and Physics), along with evidence of effective teaching at the undergraduate or graduate level. Generally, individuals with a doctoral degree are eligible to teach graduate or undergraduate courses; individuals with a master\u2019s degree are eligible to teach undergraduate courses. Please submit via PDF file (a) a letter of application summarizing your teaching qualifications, (b) your curriculum vitae, including professional certifications and professional experience, and (c) contact information for two individuals who can provide letters of recommendation. West Virginia University is a place of purpose and community. We take pride in our profound impact on the state of West Virginia and are committed to the personal and professional growth of our employees. From the groundbreaking R1 research at our flagship campus in Morgantown to the career-oriented programs at WVU Potomac State in Keyser, and the technology-intensive programs at WVU Tech in Beckley, the contributions of WVU employees resonate across the state, touching lives and shaping futures. At WVU, you will discover a supportive community that champions work-life balance and fosters a collaborative atmosphere. Our core values \u2014 service, curiosity, respect, accountability and appreciation \u2014 unite us as Mountaineers. Join us at West Virginia University, where your work will make a lasting impact. To learn more about WVU, visit wvu.edu . West Virginia University is an Equal Opportunity Employer. We invite all qualified applicants regardless of race, color, religion, sex, national origin, age, disability, genetic information, or Veteran status. Contact us SHARED SERVICES CUSTOMER CARE Location : 3rd Floor, One Waterfront Place, Morgantown, WV 26501 Phone : (304)-293-6006 Email : sharedservices@mail.wvu.edu Get directions to our office Hours Of Operation Monday - Friday 8 a.m. - 5 p.m. Support by Phone Call: 8 a.m. - 5 p.m. Support by Online Chat: Excluding University holidays Accreditations Web Standards Questions or Comments? \u00a9 2025 West Virginia University. West Virginia University is an Equal Opportunity Employer. Last updated on March 6, 2025. A-Z Site Index Campus Map Jobs Directory Give MyAccess MountaineerTRAK WVU Alert WVU Today WVU Portal WVU on Facebook WVU on Twitter WVU on YouTube"}, "https://wvu.taleo.net/careersection/faculty/jobdetail.ftl?job=28953&lang=en": {"title": "Part-time Adjunct Teaching Positions - Program for Leadership Studies", "description": "Job Description - Part-time Adjunct Teaching Positions - Program for Leadership Studies (28953) Go to the main content section. Skip to main content Careers Talent and Culture Required Postings WVU Home Home Career Opportunities Why WVU Community Information WVU Talent Network Welcome. You are not signed in. | My Account Options My Job Cart | Sign In This service is set to disconnect automatically after {0} minutes of inactivity. Your session will end in {1} minutes. Click OK to reset the timer to {0} minutes. You have been signed out. This service is set to sign out after {0} minutes of inactivity. Job Search My Jobpage Basic Search | Advanced Search | Beginning of the main content section. Return to the home page Printable Format Job Description - Part-time Adjunct Teaching Positions - Program for Leadership Studies (28953) Part-time Adjunct Teaching Positions - Program for Leadership Studies - 28953 Description The Program in Leadership Studies ( https://leadershipstudies.wvu.edu/ ) at West Virginia University invites applications for Part-time Adjunct Teaching Positions. Areas of need include, but may not be limited to, courses in Principles of Leadership, Problems in Leadership, and others. The successful candidate will be responsible for teaching in-person or online courses in the Program in Leadership Studies\u2019 undergraduate and graduate programs. Applications will be accepted throughout the year and will be considered as openings arise. Salary is established on a per-course basis. Qualifications These positions require a master\u2019s or doctoral degree in Leadership, Educational Leadership, or a closely related discipline, along with evidence of effective teaching at the undergraduate or graduate level. Generally, individuals with a doctoral degree are eligible to teach graduate or undergraduate courses; individuals with a master\u2019s degree are eligible to teach undergraduate courses. Please submit via PDF file (a) a letter of application summarizing your teaching qualifications, (b) your curriculum vitae, including professional certifications and professional experience, and (c) contact information for two individuals who can provide letters of recommendation. West Virginia University is a place of purpose and community. We take pride in our profound impact on the state of West Virginia and are committed to the personal and professional growth of our employees. From the groundbreaking R1 research at our flagship campus in Morgantown to the career-oriented programs at WVU Potomac State in Keyser, and the technology-intensive programs at WVU Tech in Beckley, the contributions of WVU employees resonate across the state, touching lives and shaping futures. At WVU, you will discover a supportive community that champions work-life balance and fosters a collaborative atmosphere. Our core values \u2014 service, curiosity, respect, accountability and appreciation \u2014 unite us as Mountaineers. Join us at West Virginia University, where your work will make a lasting impact. To learn more about WVU, visit wvu.edu . West Virginia University is an Equal Opportunity Employer. We invite all qualified applicants regardless of race, color, religion, sex, national origin, age, disability, genetic information, or Veteran status. Contact us SHARED SERVICES CUSTOMER CARE Location : 3rd Floor, One Waterfront Place, Morgantown, WV 26501 Phone : (304)-293-6006 Email : sharedservices@mail.wvu.edu Get directions to our office Hours Of Operation Monday - Friday 8 a.m. - 5 p.m. Support by Phone Call: 8 a.m. - 5 p.m. Support by Online Chat: Excluding University holidays Accreditations Web Standards Questions or Comments? \u00a9 2025 West Virginia University. West Virginia University is an Equal Opportunity Employer. Last updated on March 6, 2025. A-Z Site Index Campus Map Jobs Directory Give MyAccess MountaineerTRAK WVU Alert WVU Today WVU Portal WVU on Facebook WVU on Twitter WVU on YouTube"}, "https://wvu.taleo.net/careersection/faculty/jobdetail.ftl?job=28983&lang=en": {"title": "Adjunct Faculty - Department of Mechanical, Materials and Aerospace Engineering", "description": "Job Description - Adjunct Faculty - Department of Mechanical, Materials and Aerospace Engineering (28983) Go to the main content section. Skip to main content Careers Talent and Culture Required Postings WVU Home Home Career Opportunities Why WVU Community Information WVU Talent Network Welcome. You are not signed in. | My Account Options My Job Cart | Sign In This service is set to disconnect automatically after {0} minutes of inactivity. Your session will end in {1} minutes. Click OK to reset the timer to {0} minutes. You have been signed out. This service is set to sign out after {0} minutes of inactivity. Job Search My Jobpage Basic Search | Advanced Search | Beginning of the main content section. Return to the home page Printable Format Job Description - Adjunct Faculty - Department of Mechanical, Materials and Aerospace Engineering (28983) Adjunct Faculty - Department of Mechanical, Materials and Aerospace Engineering - 28983 Description The Benjamin M. Statler College of Engineering and Mineral Resources at West Virginia University (WVU) invites applications for adjunct faculty positions. The appointment shall be in the Department of Mechanical, Materials and Aerospace Engineering. Applicants whose interests and expertise align with departmental most critical teaching needs including solid mechanics, dynamics and control, energy systems, and mechatronics are specifically encouraged to apply. West Virginia University is designated an R1 University (Highest Research Activity) by the Carnegie Classification of Institutions of Higher Education. The Statler College is growing and currently has seven academic departments, over 3,200 students, and 135 faculty members. The Department of Mechanical, Materials and Aerospace Engineering (MMAE) has 30 faculty members and approximately 600 undergraduate students and 100 graduate students. The department annual research expenditures exceeded $14 million in the last fiscal year. Our educational programs place a strong emphasis on experiential learning in its undergraduate programs boasting numerous top 10 placements in national or international student competitions in recent years. For example, our Experimental Rocketry and EcoCAR teams have secured numerous top placements. Likewise, the WVU Robotics program has a strong track record of success winning 9 national or international robotics competitions since 2011 and $900K in prize from NASA Centennial Challenges. The Department houses undergraduate and graduate programs in Mechanical Engineering and Aerospace Engineering, graduate programs in Materials Science Engineering, and starting in Fall 2024, the department launched Bachelor of Science Robotics Engineering in partnership with the Lane Department of Computer Science and Electrical Engineering in the Statler College. Morgantown lies within a high technology corridor that includes several federal research facilities, such as the NASA Katherine Johnson Independent Verification and Validation Facility (IV&V), U.S. Department of Energy's National Energy Technology Laboratory (NETL), the National Institute of Occupational Safety and Health (NIOSH), and the Federal Bureau of Investigation (FBI). Additional details on the area and the university are available at http://www.morgantownwv.gov and http://www.wvu.edu . Morgantown is a safe, inclusive, and family-friendly community and is ranked among the most livable small cities in the country with a close proximity to Pittsburgh, PA, and Washington, DC. WVU provides faculty members with a supportive environment for developing a visible and productive career and a range of progressive policies to support work-life integration. WVU also offers a Dual Career Program to assist partners in their career transition and job search. Qualifications Eligible candidates must hold an earned Doctorate degree in mechanical engineering, aerospace engineering, materials engineering, robotics engineering, or a closely related field, at the time of appointment. The successful candidates must demonstrate the ability or potential (1) teach and develop a variety of courses at both the undergraduate and graduate levels and (2) perform professional service activities within and outside the university. A notable record past teaching experiences and scholarly activity is preferred and effective communication skills are required. To apply for this position, visit https://careers.wvu.edu/career-opportunities . Applicants must submit a cover letter that indicates the candidate's specialty area of interest, a curriculum vitae, a two-page statement of teaching philosophy, and the contact information for at least three professional references. Review of applica tions will begin immediately and continue until filled. For further information, please contact Dr. Jason Gross, Chair of the MMAE Department, by e-mail (jason.gross@mail.wvu.edu), or visit our website at https://mmae.statler.wvu.edu/ . West Virginia University is a place of purpose and community. We take pride in our profound impact on the state of West Virginia and are committed to the personal and professional growth of our employees. From the groundbreaking R1 research at our flagship campus in Morgantown to the career-oriented programs at WVU Potomac State in Keyser, and the technology-intensive programs at WVU Tech in Beckley, the contributions of WVU employees resonate across the state, touching lives and shaping futures. At WVU, you will discover a supportive community that champions work-life balance and fosters a collaborative atmosphere. Our core values \u2014 service, curiosity, respect, accountability and appreciation \u2014 unite us as Mountaineers. Join us at West Virginia University, where your work will make a lasting impact. To learn more about WVU, visit wvu.edu . West Virginia University is an Equal Opportunity Employer. We invite all qualified applicants regardless of race, color, religion, sex, national origin, age, disability, genetic information, or Veteran status. Contact us SHARED SERVICES CUSTOMER CARE Location : 3rd Floor, One Waterfront Place, Morgantown, WV 26501 Phone : (304)-293-6006 Email : sharedservices@mail.wvu.edu Get directions to our office Hours Of Operation Monday - Friday 8 a.m. - 5 p.m. Support by Phone Call: 8 a.m. - 5 p.m. Support by Online Chat: Excluding University holidays Accreditations Web Standards Questions or Comments? \u00a9 2025 West Virginia University. West Virginia University is an Equal Opportunity Employer. Last updated on March 6, 2025. A-Z Site Index Campus Map Jobs Directory Give MyAccess MountaineerTRAK WVU Alert WVU Today WVU Portal WVU on Facebook WVU on Twitter WVU on YouTube"}, "https://wvu.taleo.net/careersection/faculty/jobdetail.ftl?job=28964&lang=en": {"title": "Part-time Adjunct Teaching Positions - Programs in Multi and Interdisciplinary Studies", "description": "Job Description - Part-time Adjunct Teaching Positions - Programs in Multi and Interdisciplinary Studies (28964) Go to the main content section. Skip to main content Careers Talent and Culture Required Postings WVU Home Home Career Opportunities Why WVU Community Information WVU Talent Network Welcome. You are not signed in. | My Account Options My Job Cart | Sign In This service is set to disconnect automatically after {0} minutes of inactivity. Your session will end in {1} minutes. Click OK to reset the timer to {0} minutes. You have been signed out. This service is set to sign out after {0} minutes of inactivity. Job Search My Jobpage Basic Search | Advanced Search | Beginning of the main content section. Return to the home page Printable Format Job Description - Part-time Adjunct Teaching Positions - Programs in Multi and Interdisciplinary Studies (28964) Part-time Adjunct Teaching Positions - Programs in Multi and Interdisciplinary Studies - 28964 Description The Programs in Multi and Interdisciplinary Studies ( https://mds.wvu.edu/ ) at West Virginia University invites applications for Part-time Adjunct Teaching Positions. Areas of need include, may not be limited to, orientation-level courses, writing intensive courses, and portfolio development. The successful candidate will be responsible for teaching in-person or online courses in the Programs in Multi and Interdisciplinary Studies\u2019 undergraduate and graduate programs. Applications will be accepted throughout the year and will be considered as openings arise. Salary is established on a per-course basis. Qualifications These positions require a master\u2019s or doctoral degree in Liberal Arts, Social Sciences, or Interdisciplinary Studies or a closely related discipline, along with evidence of effective teaching at the undergraduate or graduate level. Generally, individuals with a doctoral degree are eligible to teach graduate or undergraduate courses; individuals with a master\u2019s degree are eligible to teach undergraduate courses. Experience teaching online courses is desirable. Please submit via PDF file (a) a letter of application summarizing your teaching qualifications, (b) your curriculum vitae, including professional certifications and professional experience, and (c) contact information for two individuals who can provide letters of recommendation. West Virginia University is a place of purpose and community. We take pride in our profound impact on the state of West Virginia and are committed to the personal and professional growth of our employees. From the groundbreaking R1 research at our flagship campus in Morgantown to the career-oriented programs at WVU Potomac State in Keyser, and the technology-intensive programs at WVU Tech in Beckley, the contributions of WVU employees resonate across the state, touching lives and shaping futures. At WVU, you will discover a supportive community that champions work-life balance and fosters a collaborative atmosphere. Our core values \u2014 service, curiosity, respect, accountability and appreciation \u2014 unite us as Mountaineers. Join us at West Virginia University, where your work will make a lasting impact. To learn more about WVU, visit wvu.edu . West Virginia University is an Equal Opportunity Employer. We invite all qualified applicants regardless of race, color, religion, sex, national origin, age, disability, genetic information, or Veteran status. Contact us SHARED SERVICES CUSTOMER CARE Location : 3rd Floor, One Waterfront Place, Morgantown, WV 26501 Phone : (304)-293-6006 Email : sharedservices@mail.wvu.edu Get directions to our office Hours Of Operation Monday - Friday 8 a.m. - 5 p.m. Support by Phone Call: 8 a.m. - 5 p.m. Support by Online Chat: Excluding University holidays Accreditations Web Standards Questions or Comments? \u00a9 2025 West Virginia University. West Virginia University is an Equal Opportunity Employer. Last updated on March 6, 2025. A-Z Site Index Campus Map Jobs Directory Give MyAccess MountaineerTRAK WVU Alert WVU Today WVU Portal WVU on Facebook WVU on Twitter WVU on YouTube"}, "https://wvu.taleo.net/careersection/faculty/jobdetail.ftl?job=28961&lang=en": {"title": "Part-time Adjunct Teaching Positions - Department of Geology and Geography", "description": "Job Description - Part-time Adjunct Teaching Positions - Department of Geology and Geography (28961) Go to the main content section. Skip to main content Careers Talent and Culture Required Postings WVU Home Home Career Opportunities Why WVU Community Information WVU Talent Network Welcome. You are not signed in. | My Account Options My Job Cart | Sign In This service is set to disconnect automatically after {0} minutes of inactivity. Your session will end in {1} minutes. Click OK to reset the timer to {0} minutes. You have been signed out. This service is set to sign out after {0} minutes of inactivity. Job Search My Jobpage Basic Search | Advanced Search | Beginning of the main content section. Return to the home page Printable Format Job Description - Part-time Adjunct Teaching Positions - Department of Geology and Geography (28961) Part-time Adjunct Teaching Positions - Department of Geology and Geography - 28961 Description The Department of Geology and Geography ( https://www.geo.wvu.edu/ ) at West Virginia University invites applications for Part-time Adjunct Teaching Positions. Areas of need include, may not be limited to, Geographic Information Science (GIS), Remote Sensing, Data Analytics, Field Geology and Subsurface Geology. The successful candidate will be responsible for teaching in-person or online courses in the Department of Geology and Geography\u2019s undergraduate and graduate programs. Applications will be accepted throughout the year and will be considered as openings arise. Salary is established on a per-course basis. Qualifications These positions require a master\u2019s or doctoral degree in Geology, Geography or a closely related discipline, along with evidence of effective teaching at the undergraduate or graduate level. Generally, individuals with a doctoral degree are eligible to teach graduate or undergraduate courses; individuals with a master\u2019s degree are eligible to teach undergraduate courses. Please submit via PDF file (a) a letter of application summarizing your teaching qualifications, (b) your curriculum vitae, including professional certifications and professional experience, and (c) contact information for two individuals who can provide letters of recommendation. West Virginia University is a place of purpose and community. We take pride in our profound impact on the state of West Virginia and are committed to the personal and professional growth of our employees. From the groundbreaking R1 research at our flagship campus in Morgantown to the career-oriented programs at WVU Potomac State in Keyser, and the technology-intensive programs at WVU Tech in Beckley, the contributions of WVU employees resonate across the state, touching lives and shaping futures. At WVU, you will discover a supportive community that champions work-life balance and fosters a collaborative atmosphere. Our core values \u2014 service, curiosity, respect, accountability and appreciation \u2014 unite us as Mountaineers. Join us at West Virginia University, where your work will make a lasting impact. To learn more about WVU, visit wvu.edu . West Virginia University is an Equal Opportunity Employer. We invite all qualified applicants regardless of race, color, religion, sex, national origin, age, disability, genetic information, or Veteran status. Contact us SHARED SERVICES CUSTOMER CARE Location : 3rd Floor, One Waterfront Place, Morgantown, WV 26501 Phone : (304)-293-6006 Email : sharedservices@mail.wvu.edu Get directions to our office Hours Of Operation Monday - Friday 8 a.m. - 5 p.m. Support by Phone Call: 8 a.m. - 5 p.m. Support by Online Chat: Excluding University holidays Accreditations Web Standards Questions or Comments? \u00a9 2025 West Virginia University. West Virginia University is an Equal Opportunity Employer. Last updated on March 6, 2025. A-Z Site Index Campus Map Jobs Directory Give MyAccess MountaineerTRAK WVU Alert WVU Today WVU Portal WVU on Facebook WVU on Twitter WVU on YouTube"}, "https://wvu.taleo.net/careersection/faculty/jobdetail.ftl?job=28958&lang=en": {"title": "Part-time Adjunct Teaching Positions - Department of Biology", "description": "Job Description - Part-time Adjunct Teaching Positions - Department of Biology (28958) Go to the main content section. Skip to main content Careers Talent and Culture Required Postings WVU Home Home Career Opportunities Why WVU Community Information WVU Talent Network Welcome. You are not signed in. | My Account Options My Job Cart | Sign In This service is set to disconnect automatically after {0} minutes of inactivity. Your session will end in {1} minutes. Click OK to reset the timer to {0} minutes. You have been signed out. This service is set to sign out after {0} minutes of inactivity. Job Search My Jobpage Basic Search | Advanced Search | Beginning of the main content section. Return to the home page Printable Format Job Description - Part-time Adjunct Teaching Positions - Department of Biology (28958) Part-time Adjunct Teaching Positions - Department of Biology - 28958 Description The Department of Biology ( https://biology.wvu.edu ) at West Virginia University invites applications for Part-time Adjunct Teaching Positions. The successful candidate will be responsible for teaching in-person or online courses in the Department of Biology\u2019s undergraduate and graduate programs. Applications will be accepted throughout the year and will be considered as openings arise. Salary is established on a per-course basis. Qualifications These positions require a master\u2019s or doctoral degree in Biology or a closely related discipline, along with evidence of effective teaching at the undergraduate or graduate level. Generally, individuals with a doctoral degree are eligible to teach graduate or undergraduate courses; individuals with a master\u2019s degree are eligible to teach undergraduate courses. Please submit via PDF file (a) a letter of application summarizing your teaching qualifications, (b) your curriculum vitae, including professional certifications and professional experience, and (c) contact information for two individuals who can provide letters of recommendation. West Virginia University is a place of purpose and community. We take pride in our profound impact on the state of West Virginia and are committed to the personal and professional growth of our employees. From the groundbreaking R1 research at our flagship campus in Morgantown to the career-oriented programs at WVU Potomac State in Keyser, and the technology-intensive programs at WVU Tech in Beckley, the contributions of WVU employees resonate across the state, touching lives and shaping futures. At WVU, you will discover a supportive community that champions work-life balance and fosters a collaborative atmosphere. Our core values \u2014 service, curiosity, respect, accountability and appreciation \u2014 unite us as Mountaineers. Join us at West Virginia University, where your work will make a lasting impact. To learn more about WVU, visit wvu.edu . West Virginia University is an Equal Opportunity Employer. We invite all qualified applicants regardless of race, color, religion, sex, national origin, age, disability, genetic information, or Veteran status. Contact us SHARED SERVICES CUSTOMER CARE Location : 3rd Floor, One Waterfront Place, Morgantown, WV 26501 Phone : (304)-293-6006 Email : sharedservices@mail.wvu.edu Get directions to our office Hours Of Operation Monday - Friday 8 a.m. - 5 p.m. Support by Phone Call: 8 a.m. - 5 p.m. Support by Online Chat: Excluding University holidays Accreditations Web Standards Questions or Comments? \u00a9 2025 West Virginia University. West Virginia University is an Equal Opportunity Employer. Last updated on March 6, 2025. A-Z Site Index Campus Map Jobs Directory Give MyAccess MountaineerTRAK WVU Alert WVU Today WVU Portal WVU on Facebook WVU on Twitter WVU on YouTube"}, "https://wvu.taleo.net/careersection/faculty/jobdetail.ftl?job=28985&lang=en": {"title": "Part-time Clinic Adjunct Faculty \u2013 College of Law ", "description": "Job Description - Part-time Clinic Adjunct Faculty \u2013 College of Law  (28985) Go to the main content section. Skip to main content Careers Talent and Culture Required Postings WVU Home Home Career Opportunities Why WVU Community Information WVU Talent Network Welcome. You are not signed in. | My Account Options My Job Cart | Sign In This service is set to disconnect automatically after {0} minutes of inactivity. Your session will end in {1} minutes. Click OK to reset the timer to {0} minutes. You have been signed out. This service is set to sign out after {0} minutes of inactivity. Job Search My Jobpage Basic Search | Advanced Search | Beginning of the main content section. Return to the home page Printable Format Job Description - Part-time Clinic Adjunct Faculty \u2013 College of Law  (28985) Part-time Clinic Adjunct Faculty \u2013 College of Law - 28985 Description The College of Law at West Virginia University invites applications for part-time adjunct faculty positions to supervise students representing clients in the clinical law program in various areas of law. Applicants should have demonstrated expertise and practice experience in the area of law for the clinics in which they will supervise students and be committed to providing a rigorous and quality educational experiences to our students while ensuring competent representation of clients. Clinic adjuncts typically supervise one or two teams of students each semester and are asked to commit to supervising these teams for both semesters in the academic year; each team consists of two students and the composition of the teams will remain the same for both semesters. Essential duties include: Working collaboratively with clinical law faculty and staff; Ensuring effective and diligent case management for all assigned cases; Traveling to meetings and court proceedings as necessary; Contributing to and maintaining a positive and collaborative learning environment; Ensuring that students receive prompt and productive feedback concerning their work; Being available and responsive to students; Being aware of and following academic policies and procedures related to instruction and recordkeeping; Attending all required adjunct faculty training and other meetings during the semester. Qualifications These positions require applicants to have a J.D. degree, an active bar license and admission to the applicable court(s) in which the clinic represents clients, evidence of being in good standing with the appropriate state or federal bar, and a minimum of three years of professional legal experience. Additionally, the following qualifications are strongly preferred: Supervisory experience in a legal practice setting. A record of engagement with the College of Law. A judicial clerkship or similar experience. Applications will be accepted throughout the year and will be considered as openings arise. Salary is established on a per-team basis. Appointments will be for a specified term and renewal of the position will be based on course need. These positions are not benefits eligible. Please submit the following: (1) a letter of application summarizing your area of expertise and teaching interest and qualifications; (2) your curriculum vitae; (3) contact information for two professional references. West Virginia University is a place of purpose and community. We take pride in our profound impact on the state of West Virginia and are committed to the personal and professional growth of our employees. From the groundbreaking R1 research at our flagship campus in Morgantown to the career-oriented programs at WVU Potomac State in Keyser, and the technology-intensive programs at WVU Tech in Beckley, the contributions of WVU employees resonate across the state, touching lives and shaping futures. At WVU, you will discover a supportive community that champions work-life balance and fosters a collaborative atmosphere. Our core values \u2014 service, curiosity, respect, accountability and appreciation \u2014 unite us as Mountaineers. Join us at West Virginia University, where your work will make a lasting impact. To learn more about WVU, visit wvu.edu . West Virginia University is an Equal Opportunity Employer. We invite all qualified applicants regardless of race, color, religion, sex, national origin, age, disability, genetic information, or Veteran status. Contact us SHARED SERVICES CUSTOMER CARE Location : 3rd Floor, One Waterfront Place, Morgantown, WV 26501 Phone : (304)-293-6006 Email : sharedservices@mail.wvu.edu Get directions to our office Hours Of Operation Monday - Friday 8 a.m. - 5 p.m. Support by Phone Call: 8 a.m. - 5 p.m. Support by Online Chat: Excluding University holidays Accreditations Web Standards Questions or Comments? \u00a9 2025 West Virginia University. West Virginia University is an Equal Opportunity Employer. Last updated on March 6, 2025. A-Z Site Index Campus Map Jobs Directory Give MyAccess MountaineerTRAK WVU Alert WVU Today WVU Portal WVU on Facebook WVU on Twitter WVU on YouTube"}, "https://wvu.taleo.net/careersection/faculty/jobdetail.ftl?job=28972&lang=en": {"title": "Part-time Adjunct Teaching Positions - Department of Forensic and Investigative Science", "description": "Job Description - Part-time Adjunct Teaching Positions - Department of Forensic and Investigative Science (28972) Go to the main content section. Skip to main content Careers Talent and Culture Required Postings WVU Home Home Career Opportunities Why WVU Community Information WVU Talent Network Welcome. You are not signed in. | My Account Options My Job Cart | Sign In This service is set to disconnect automatically after {0} minutes of inactivity. Your session will end in {1} minutes. Click OK to reset the timer to {0} minutes. You have been signed out. This service is set to sign out after {0} minutes of inactivity. Job Search My Jobpage Basic Search | Advanced Search | Beginning of the main content section. Return to the home page Printable Format Job Description - Part-time Adjunct Teaching Positions - Department of Forensic and Investigative Science (28972) Part-time Adjunct Teaching Positions - Department of Forensic and Investigative Science - 28972 Description The Department of Forensic and Investigative Science ( https://forensics.wvu.edu ) at West Virginia University invites applications for Part-time Adjunct Teaching Positions. Areas of need include, may not be limited to, Introduction to Microscopy, Latent Fingerprint Examination, Crime Scene Investigation, Firearm and Toolmark Examination, Forensic Toxicology, Forensic Drug Analyses, Forensic Arson Chemistry, Forensic Trace Analyses, Forensic Serology and DNA analyses. The successful candidate will be responsible for teaching in-person or online courses in the Department of Forensic and Investigative Science\u2019s undergraduate and graduate programs. Applications will be accepted throughout the year and will be considered as openings arise. Salary is established on a per-course basis. Qualifications These positions require a master\u2019s or doctoral degree in Forensic and Investigative Science or a closely related discipline, along with evidence of effective teaching at the undergraduate or graduate level. Generally, individuals with a doctoral degree are eligible to teach graduate or undergraduate courses; individuals with a master\u2019s degree are eligible to teach undergraduate courses. Please submit via PDF file (a) a letter of application summarizing your teaching qualifications, (b) your curriculum vitae, including professional certifications and professional experience, and (c) contact information for two individuals who can provide letters of recommendation. West Virginia University is a place of purpose and community. We take pride in our profound impact on the state of West Virginia and are committed to the personal and professional growth of our employees. From the groundbreaking R1 research at our flagship campus in Morgantown to the career-oriented programs at WVU Potomac State in Keyser, and the technology-intensive programs at WVU Tech in Beckley, the contributions of WVU employees resonate across the state, touching lives and shaping futures. At WVU, you will discover a supportive community that champions work-life balance and fosters a collaborative atmosphere. Our core values \u2014 service, curiosity, respect, accountability and appreciation \u2014 unite us as Mountaineers. Join us at West Virginia University, where your work will make a lasting impact. To learn more about WVU, visit wvu.edu . West Virginia University is an Equal Opportunity Employer. We invite all qualified applicants regardless of race, color, religion, sex, national origin, age, disability, genetic information, or Veteran status. Contact us SHARED SERVICES CUSTOMER CARE Location : 3rd Floor, One Waterfront Place, Morgantown, WV 26501 Phone : (304)-293-6006 Email : sharedservices@mail.wvu.edu Get directions to our office Hours Of Operation Monday - Friday 8 a.m. - 5 p.m. Support by Phone Call: 8 a.m. - 5 p.m. Support by Online Chat: Excluding University holidays Accreditations Web Standards Questions or Comments? \u00a9 2025 West Virginia University. West Virginia University is an Equal Opportunity Employer. Last updated on March 6, 2025. A-Z Site Index Campus Map Jobs Directory Give MyAccess MountaineerTRAK WVU Alert WVU Today WVU Portal WVU on Facebook WVU on Twitter WVU on YouTube"}, "https://wvu.taleo.net/careersection/faculty/jobdetail.ftl?job=28959&lang=en": {"title": "Part-time Adjunct Teaching Positions - Department of Communication Studies", "description": "Job Description - Part-time Adjunct Teaching Positions - Department of Communication Studies (28959) Go to the main content section. Skip to main content Careers Talent and Culture Required Postings WVU Home Home Career Opportunities Why WVU Community Information WVU Talent Network Welcome. You are not signed in. | My Account Options My Job Cart | Sign In This service is set to disconnect automatically after {0} minutes of inactivity. Your session will end in {1} minutes. Click OK to reset the timer to {0} minutes. You have been signed out. This service is set to sign out after {0} minutes of inactivity. Job Search My Jobpage Basic Search | Advanced Search | Beginning of the main content section. Return to the home page Printable Format Job Description - Part-time Adjunct Teaching Positions - Department of Communication Studies (28959) Part-time Adjunct Teaching Positions - Department of Communication Studies - 28959 Description The Department of Communication Studies ( https://communicationstudies.wvu.edu/ ) at West Virginia University invites applications for Part-time Adjunct Teaching Positions. Areas of need include, may not be limited to, mediated and mass communication, small group communication, health communication, organizational communication, nonverbal communication, and persuasion. The successful candidate will be responsible for teaching in-person or online courses in the Department of Communication Studies\u2019 undergraduate and graduate programs. Applications will be accepted throughout the year and will be considered as openings arise. Salary is established on a per-course basis. Qualifications These positions require a master\u2019s or doctoral degree in Communication Studies or a closely related discipline, along with evidence of effective teaching at the undergraduate or graduate level. Generally, individuals with a doctoral degree are eligible to teach graduate or undergraduate courses; individuals with a master\u2019s degree are eligible to teach undergraduate courses. Applicants should have experience teaching large lectures courses or online courses. Please submit via PDF file (a) a letter of application summarizing your teaching qualifications, (b) your curriculum vitae, including professional certifications and professional experience, and (c) contact information for two individuals who can provide letters of recommendation. West Virginia University is a place of purpose and community. We take pride in our profound impact on the state of West Virginia and are committed to the personal and professional growth of our employees. From the groundbreaking R1 research at our flagship campus in Morgantown to the career-oriented programs at WVU Potomac State in Keyser, and the technology-intensive programs at WVU Tech in Beckley, the contributions of WVU employees resonate across the state, touching lives and shaping futures. At WVU, you will discover a supportive community that champions work-life balance and fosters a collaborative atmosphere. Our core values \u2014 service, curiosity, respect, accountability and appreciation \u2014 unite us as Mountaineers. Join us at West Virginia University, where your work will make a lasting impact. To learn more about WVU, visit wvu.edu . West Virginia University is an Equal Opportunity Employer. We invite all qualified applicants regardless of race, color, religion, sex, national origin, age, disability, genetic information, or Veteran status. Contact us SHARED SERVICES CUSTOMER CARE Location : 3rd Floor, One Waterfront Place, Morgantown, WV 26501 Phone : (304)-293-6006 Email : sharedservices@mail.wvu.edu Get directions to our office Hours Of Operation Monday - Friday 8 a.m. - 5 p.m. Support by Phone Call: 8 a.m. - 5 p.m. Support by Online Chat: Excluding University holidays Accreditations Web Standards Questions or Comments? \u00a9 2025 West Virginia University. West Virginia University is an Equal Opportunity Employer. Last updated on March 6, 2025. A-Z Site Index Campus Map Jobs Directory Give MyAccess MountaineerTRAK WVU Alert WVU Today WVU Portal WVU on Facebook WVU on Twitter WVU on YouTube"}, "https://wvu.taleo.net/careersection/faculty/jobdetail.ftl?job=28965&lang=en": {"title": "Part-time Adjunct Teaching Positions - Department of Philosophy and Program for Religious Studies ", "description": "Job Description - Part-time Adjunct Teaching Positions - Department of Philosophy and Program for Religious Studies  (28965) Go to the main content section. Skip to main content Careers Talent and Culture Required Postings WVU Home Home Career Opportunities Why WVU Community Information WVU Talent Network Welcome. You are not signed in. | My Account Options My Job Cart | Sign In This service is set to disconnect automatically after {0} minutes of inactivity. Your session will end in {1} minutes. Click OK to reset the timer to {0} minutes. You have been signed out. This service is set to sign out after {0} minutes of inactivity. Job Search My Jobpage Basic Search | Advanced Search | Beginning of the main content section. Return to the home page Printable Format Job Description - Part-time Adjunct Teaching Positions - Department of Philosophy and Program for Religious Studies  (28965) Part-time Adjunct Teaching Positions - Department of Philosophy and Program for Religious Studies - 28965 Description The Eberly College of Arts and Sciences at West Virginia University is currently inviting applications for Part-time Adjunct Teaching Positions in the Department of Philosophy ( https://philosophy.wvu.edu ) and the Program for Religious Studies ( https://religiousstudies.wvu.edu/ ). Areas of need include, but are not limited to, Current Moral Issues; Introduction to World Religions; History and Practice of Christianity; and History and Practice of Islam. The successful candidate will be responsible for teaching in-person or online courses in the Department of Philosophy or in the Program for Religious Studies. Generally, individuals with a doctoral degree are eligible to teach graduate or undergraduate courses; individuals with a master\u2019s degree are eligible to teach undergraduate courses. Applications will be accepted throughout the year and will be considered as openings arise. Salary is established on a per-course basis. Qualifications Philosophy: The positions for the Department of Philosophy require a master\u2019s or doctoral degree in Philosophy or a closely related discipline. Program for Religious Studies: The positions for the Program for Religious Studies require a master\u2019s or doctoral degree in Religious Studies or a closely related discipline. For all positions, evidence of effective teaching at the undergraduate or graduate level is required. Please submit via PDF file (a) a letter of application summarizing your teaching qualifications, (b) your curriculum vitae, including professional certifications and professional experience, and (c) contact information for two individuals who can provide letters of recommendation. West Virginia University is a place of purpose and community. We take pride in our profound impact on the state of West Virginia and are committed to the personal and professional growth of our employees. From the groundbreaking R1 research at our flagship campus in Morgantown to the career-oriented programs at WVU Potomac State in Keyser, and the technology-intensive programs at WVU Tech in Beckley, the contributions of WVU employees resonate across the state, touching lives and shaping futures. At WVU, you will discover a supportive community that champions work-life balance and fosters a collaborative atmosphere. Our core values \u2014 service, curiosity, respect, accountability and appreciation \u2014 unite us as Mountaineers. Join us at West Virginia University, where your work will make a lasting impact. To learn more about WVU, visit wvu.edu . West Virginia University is an Equal Opportunity Employer. We invite all qualified applicants regardless of race, color, religion, sex, national origin, age, disability, genetic information, or Veteran status. Contact us SHARED SERVICES CUSTOMER CARE Location : 3rd Floor, One Waterfront Place, Morgantown, WV 26501 Phone : (304)-293-6006 Email : sharedservices@mail.wvu.edu Get directions to our office Hours Of Operation Monday - Friday 8 a.m. - 5 p.m. Support by Phone Call: 8 a.m. - 5 p.m. Support by Online Chat: Excluding University holidays Accreditations Web Standards Questions or Comments? \u00a9 2025 West Virginia University. West Virginia University is an Equal Opportunity Employer. Last updated on March 6, 2025. A-Z Site Index Campus Map Jobs Directory Give MyAccess MountaineerTRAK WVU Alert WVU Today WVU Portal WVU on Facebook WVU on Twitter WVU on YouTube"}, "https://wvu.taleo.net/careersection/faculty/jobdetail.ftl?job=28981&lang=en": {"title": "Adjunct Instructor - Accounting - John Chambers College of Business and Economics", "description": "Job Description - Adjunct Instructor - Accounting - John Chambers College of Business and Economics (28981) Go to the main content section. Skip to main content Careers Talent and Culture Required Postings WVU Home Home Career Opportunities Why WVU Community Information WVU Talent Network Welcome. You are not signed in. | My Account Options My Job Cart | Sign In This service is set to disconnect automatically after {0} minutes of inactivity. Your session will end in {1} minutes. Click OK to reset the timer to {0} minutes. You have been signed out. This service is set to sign out after {0} minutes of inactivity. Job Search My Jobpage Basic Search | Advanced Search | Beginning of the main content section. Return to the home page Printable Format Job Description - Adjunct Instructor - Accounting - John Chambers College of Business and Economics (28981) Adjunct Instructor - Accounting - John Chambers College of Business and Economics - 28981 Description The Department of Accounting ( https://business.wvu.edu/academics/accounting-department/accounting ) at West Virginia University invites applications for part-time Adjunct Instructor positions. Areas of need include undergraduate and graduate courses in Accounting. Qualifications The position in accounting requires a master\u2019s degree in accounting or accounting information systems, or a PhD in Accounting -a JD may also be accepted for specific course needs. Candidates with a Bachelors agree who also hold relevant professional certifications (Certified Public Accountant \u2013 CPA, CIA, CMA, CFE) with a minimum of 10 years\u2019 experience may also be considered. Individuals with a doctoral degree are eligible to teach graduate or undergraduate courses; individuals with only a master\u2019s degree are eligible to teach undergraduate courses. Applications will be accepted throughout the year and will be considered as openings arise. Salary is established on a per-course basis. While these positions are not anticipated to be benefits-eligible, individual positions may become benefits-eligible based on course load - which may vary depending on departmental need. Please submit via PDF file (a) a letter of application summarizing your teaching qualifications, (b) your curriculum vitae, and (c) contact information for two individuals who can provide letters of recommendation. West Virginia University is a place of purpose and community. We take pride in our profound impact on the state of West Virginia and are committed to the personal and professional growth of our employees. From the groundbreaking R1 research at our flagship campus in Morgantown to the career-oriented programs at WVU Potomac State in Keyser, and the technology-intensive programs at WVU Tech in Beckley, the contributions of WVU employees resonate across the state, touching lives and shaping futures. At WVU, you will discover a supportive community that champions work-life balance and fosters a collaborative atmosphere. Our core values \u2014 service, curiosity, respect, accountability and appreciation \u2014 unite us as Mountaineers. Join us at West Virginia University, where your work will make a lasting impact. To learn more about WVU, visit wvu.edu . West Virginia University is an Equal Opportunity Employer. We invite all qualified applicants regardless of race, color, religion, sex, national origin, age, disability, genetic information, or Veteran status. Contact us SHARED SERVICES CUSTOMER CARE Location : 3rd Floor, One Waterfront Place, Morgantown, WV 26501 Phone : (304)-293-6006 Email : sharedservices@mail.wvu.edu Get directions to our office Hours Of Operation Monday - Friday 8 a.m. - 5 p.m. Support by Phone Call: 8 a.m. - 5 p.m. Support by Online Chat: Excluding University holidays Accreditations Web Standards Questions or Comments? \u00a9 2025 West Virginia University. West Virginia University is an Equal Opportunity Employer. Last updated on March 6, 2025. A-Z Site Index Campus Map Jobs Directory Give MyAccess MountaineerTRAK WVU Alert WVU Today WVU Portal WVU on Facebook WVU on Twitter WVU on YouTube"}, "https://wvu.taleo.net/careersection/faculty/jobdetail.ftl?job=28989&lang=en": {"title": "Adjunct Instructor - Finance - John Chambers College of Business and Economics ", "description": "Job Description - Adjunct Instructor - Finance - John Chambers College of Business and Economics  (28989) Go to the main content section. Skip to main content Careers Talent and Culture Required Postings WVU Home Home Career Opportunities Why WVU Community Information WVU Talent Network Welcome. You are not signed in. | My Account Options My Job Cart | Sign In This service is set to disconnect automatically after {0} minutes of inactivity. Your session will end in {1} minutes. Click OK to reset the timer to {0} minutes. You have been signed out. This service is set to sign out after {0} minutes of inactivity. Job Search My Jobpage Basic Search | Advanced Search | Beginning of the main content section. Return to the home page Printable Format Job Description - Adjunct Instructor - Finance - John Chambers College of Business and Economics  (28989) Adjunct Instructor - Finance - John Chambers College of Business and Economics - 28989 Description The Department of Finance ( https://business.wvu.edu/academics/finance-department/finance ) at West Virginia University invites applications for part-time Adjunct Instructor positions. Areas of need include undergraduate and graduate courses in finance. Qualifications The positions in finance require a master\u2019s or doctoral degree in finance or a closely related discipline and evidence of ability to teach effectively. Individuals with a doctoral degree are eligible to teach graduate or undergraduate courses; individuals with only a master\u2019s degree are eligible to teach undergraduate courses. A combination of a bachelor's degree and at least 10 years of professional experience in the finance industry may also be considered for undergraduate teaching assignments. Applications will be accepted throughout the year and will be considered as openings arise. Salary is established on a per-course basis. While these positions are not anticipated to be benefits-eligible, individual positions may become benefits-eligible based on course load - which may vary depending on departmental need. Please submit via PDF file (a) a letter of application summarizing your teaching qualifications, (b) your curriculum vitae, and (c) contact information for two individuals who can provide letters of recommendation. West Virginia University is a place of purpose and community. We take pride in our profound impact on the state of West Virginia and are committed to the personal and professional growth of our employees. From the groundbreaking R1 research at our flagship campus in Morgantown to the career-oriented programs at WVU Potomac Stat